  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MAAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MA&#x2019;AN will implement Outcomes 1 and 2 in Ramallah and Al-Bireh Governorate, focusing on integrated livelihood recovery, food security, and strengthening local and green economic systems. MA&#x2019;AN will deliver cash-for-work and land rehabilitation activitiesto provide short-term income while improving productive and community infrastructure. It will enhance food security by linking vulnerable households with local producers through integrated food assistance and by supporting small-scale farmers with inputsand Good Agricultural Practices training. In parallel, MA&#x2019;AN will support small businesses and cooperatives through technical assistance, productive asset support, financial literacy, and market linkages, while delivering market-aligned TVET and green skills training in partnership with the private sector. MA&#x2019;AN will also promote youth- and women-led innovation through Water&#x2013;Energy&#x2013;Food initiatives, piloting practical solutions that strengthen resilience and local value chains.Outcome 1: Secured basic needs and enhanced immediate livelihood opportunities -Output 1.1: Temporary employment (CfW) - Activities: (1.1.1.a) Conduct needs assessment; and bene-ficiary selection(1.1.1.b) Hire 250 unemployed individuals (at least 75 women, including youth/disabled)for infrastructure rehab (water, roads, schools). (1.1.2) Hire 500 individuals (at least 175 women, youth, smallholder farmers) for land rehabilitation. (1.1.3) Recruit 250 unem-ployed individuals to provide remedial education and business training (150 fresh graduates for remedial education- at least 100 women; 100 individuals for business training - at least 50 wom-en. Effectiveness: Provides income, builds skills, engages vulnerable groups, and strengthens food security and livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MA&apos;AN Development Center is an independent Palestinian development and training institution established in January,1989, registeredby law as a non-profit organization.  The main office is located in Ramallah and the four branch offices are located in Gaza, Khan Younis, Tulkarem  and Jenin,.  MA&apos;AN&apos;s work is informed by the necessity of creating independent, self-reliant initiatives that leadto the development of human resources for sustainable development, which incorporate values of self-sufficiency and self-empowerment.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MAAN Development Center</narrative>
